# Audit: CAPS granular hardware + net caps vs compiler gate

**Date:** 2026-08-12
**Scope:** `ooda/oodac/check_cap_util.oo` `is_cap_type()` + `std/src/net` 42 files + `std/src/hw` 5 files
**Probe:** B1-B5, C1-C5, per CAPS.oot 27 caps vs DESIGN V2 18

## Finding
- `is_cap_type()` only accepted 11 caps: NetCap, FsCap, GpuCap, ThreadCap, SysCap, EnvCap, TimeCap, RandCap, AllocCap, UnsafeFFICap, HitlCap, AuditCap
- Missing 16 granular: FsReadCap, FsWriteCap, HttpCap, TcpCap, UdpCap, BindCap, ProcessCap, SyncCap, MemCap, AudioCap, UsbCap, CameraCap, HidCap, WindowCap, FrameCap, SignCap plus FfiCap alias
- Result: `pub fn fetch(net: &HttpCap)` was ERR "unknown cap type", blocking granular adoption. 42 net files still legacy &NetCap (0 granular), 5 hw files still &SysCap stubs.

## Fix
- Updated `check_cap_util.oo:182` `is_cap_type()` to accept all 27 CAPS.oot tokens per DESIGN §3.1 + CAPS_MATRIX residual note.
- Added: FsReadCap/FsWriteCap, Http/Tcp/Udp/Bind, Process/Sync, MemCap, Audio/Camera/Usb/Hid, Window/Frame, SignCap, FfiCap alias.
- Verification: `oodac check` on `/tmp/test_httpcap.oo` now parses `&HttpCap` as valid type (no longer "unknown cap"). Enforcement still legacy: sealed `fetch` requires `&NetCap` (see `sealed_kind_of` — HttpCap not yet mapped). Next step is to map granular → legacy in `sealed_kind_of` or add `is_sealed_http` → HttpCap check.

## Residual
- `sealed_kind_of()` still returns NetCap for net fns, not HttpCap/TcpCap granularity. Per CAPS_MATRIX residual: per-op vs per-call granularity. Keep legacy NetCap for compat one wave, then migrate callers to granular with dual-support.
- 42 net files remain legacy; hw files remain stubs with &SysCap. No mass cap add this batch per RULES ≤5.

## Evidence
- `tool-outputs/9b9131b4` hw audit, `tool-outputs/03a69abc` net grep 0 granular, `tool-outputs/4396a6d7` CAPS vs product, `exec-231` HttpCap parse now green (type), `exec-232` enforcement still NetCap.
